#
# D-138 rendered: what Foundry-Liveness now does with each corruption of the
# artifacts IT ITSELF reads. Five rows, one tool, one run directory.
#
# Rows 2-4 RAISED UnicodeDecodeError across the MCP boundary before this fix,
# naming no file. NFR-002 and the house rule are one sentence here: never raise
# across MCP, refuse by name.
#
# ROW 4 IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS FOR THE CLASS. Both artifacts corrupt at once
# names BOTH, because a first-problem-wins guard is right every time and still
# costs the lead a round trip per broken file.
#
# ROW 5 IS THE CONTROL AGAINST OVER-REFUSING. A ledger is a best-effort append
# that can be interrupted mid-line; treating a half-written LINE as a corrupt
# FILE would refuse on the ordinary state of a healthy working agent, which is
# the false alarm that teaches a lead to stop reading the tool. Only bytes that
# will not DECODE are the refusal.
#
# ROW 1 IS THE CONTROL AGAINST UNDER-REPORTING: without it, "refuses when
# corrupt" is satisfied by a tool that refuses always.
#
# The refusal names the file because `read_text_file` writes the name into its
# problem string — so nothing in this module holds a list of "the artifacts
# liveness cares about". The set judged is the set read, by construction.
#

